| Category | Packages |
|----------|----------|
| Framework | `next`, `react`, `react-dom`, `next-intl`, `next-themes` |
| Types | `@types/react`, `@types/react-dom`, `@types/node` |
| Build & lint | `typescript`, `eslint`, `@tailwindcss/postcss`, `tailwindcss`, `tsx`, `prettier` |
| Testing | `vitest`, `@vitest/coverage-v8` |
| Auth (WorkOS) | `@workos-inc/authkit-nextjs`, `@workos-inc/node`, `@workos-inc/widgets`, `@workos-inc/widgets-i18n` |
| Payments (Stripe) | `stripe`, `@stripe/stripe-js` |
| Email | `resend` |
| Infrastructure | `@upstash/redis` |
| Database | `drizzle-orm` |
| UI | `@phosphor-icons/react`, `@radix-ui/themes`, `sonner`, `zod` |

## Adding a New Dependency to the Catalog

1. Check if the package is used in 2+ workspaces (or pairs with an already-cataloged dep).
2. Add it to `pnpm-workspace.yaml` under `catalog:` with the desired version range.
3. In every `package.json` that uses it, replace the semver range with `"catalog:"`.
4. Run `pnpm install` to update the lockfile.

## Upgrading a Cataloged Dependency

1. Edit the version in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` `catalog:` section.
2. Run `pnpm install`.
3. Commit both `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and `pnpm-lock.yaml`.

## Cache Invalidation

`pnpm-workspace.yaml` is listed in `turbo.json` `globalDependencies`. Any change to the catalog invalidates all Turborepo caches, ensuring builds pick up the new versions.
